50691.sol:
When light of suitable frequency falls on metal plate electrons are emitted. This effect is called photoelectric effect.<br>The maximum kinetic energy of the photo electrons depends only on frequency of the incident light. The relation is given<br>as<br>\[
K_{\max }=h f=h f_{0}
\]<br>where \( f_{0} \) is threshold frequency; \( $\mathrm{f}$\) is frequency of incident light.

53269.sol:
Let $y=x^x\Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}=x^x(1+\log x)$<br/>For increaṣing function, $\frac{d y}{d x}>0\begin{array}{cc}
\Rightarrow & x^x(1+\log x)>0 \\
\Rightarrow & 1+\log x>0 \\
\Rightarrow & \log _e x>\log _e \frac{1}{e} \\
\Rightarrow & x>\frac{1}{e}
\end{array}
$\therefore$ The function is increasing when $x>$\frac{1}{e}$

57525.sol:
Zirconium is refined by van Arkel method.
Zirconium is refined using the van Arkel technique. By heating metal in an evacuated vessel with iodine, oxygen and nitrogen present as impurities are eliminated. On a tungsten filament heated to roughly $1800 \mathrm{ K} , the metal iodide volatilizes and is degraded. On the filament, pure metal is deposited.
 \begin{array}{l}
\underset{\text{ (Impure) }}{\mathrm{Zr}}+2 \mathrm{l}_{2} \longrightarrow \mathrm{Zrl}_{4} \\
\mathrm{Zrl}_{4} \longrightarrow \underset{\text{ (Pure) }}{\mathrm{Zr}}+2 \mathrm{l}_{2}
\end{array}$
